positions retained\",\n              \"status\": \"fitz\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"fitz\",\n              \"reason\": \"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\n              \"status\": \"known_gap\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a748856a6b0d4ee03d4b7d04\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::36aa7c16dd9aa335f125602a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eec523ebb51b576f83a906d5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::336d3e9f649133c8318edf00\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用前瞻性队列研究设计。纳入标准：组织学确诊的不可切除III期或IV期皮肤黑色素瘤患者，接受抗PD-1单药治疗（纳武利尤单抗或帕博利珠单抗）。对照组为患者的直系亲属（健康人）。主要终点：根据RECIST v.1.1标准评估的治疗反应（完全缓解CR、部分缓解PR定义为响应者；疾病稳定SD、进展PD定义为非响应者）。数据采集：治疗前通过问卷收集社会人口学、临床、生活方式和饮食变量；采集基线粪便样本。实验室分析：使用DNeasy PowerSoil Pro提取DNA，扩增16S rRNA基因V3-V4区进行Illumina MiSeq测序，使用DADA2流程生成ASVs并基于SILVA数据库进行分类；对部分样本进行宏基因组鸟枪法测序以重建MAGs。统计分析：比较各组间的菌群多样性（Alpha/Beta）、相对丰度及临床特征差异，使用Kruskal-Wallis检验、Fisher精确检验及limma线性模型识别差异物种。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7ba2dfedc1eb207addb32c68\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了波兰这一特定欧洲人群背景下，肠道微生物组特征与抗PD-1治疗反应的关联证据，指出了与该人群饮食模式（如高植物摄入）相关的潜在有益菌属（P. copri, B. uniformis）。\",\n          \"limits\": \"样本量较小（尤其是对照组仅10人，且年龄显著小于患者组）；观察性研究设计无法确立因果关系；饮食数据依赖自我报告问卷，可能存在回忆偏倚；未直接测量微生物代谢产物机制；不同研究间关于特定菌属（如Faecalibacterium）作用的矛盾结果提示人群异质性，限制了单一生物标志物的普适性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3dabf81aac85365acaa0d7d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者（n=25）的拟杆菌门/厚壁菌门比值显著高于非响应者（n=32），且响应者的细菌物种丰富度（Richness）显著低于非响应者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::03ad9e12f07b47f5c940696d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者肠道中普雷沃氏菌（Prevotella copri）和均匀拟杆菌（Bacteroides uniformis）的丰度显著升高；非响应者中普拉梭菌（Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）、肠脱硫弧菌（Desulfovibrio intestinalis）及部分未分类厚壁菌显著富集。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::afb811ac51851f8ef1c79e86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线饮食调查\",\n          \"finding\": \"高植物性食物（水果和蔬菜总和）摄入与响应概率增加2.9倍相关；低乳制品摄入（每日≤1份）与响应概率增加2.0倍相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::072e088bef5b876efe98b6a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"波兰黑色素瘤患者队列，基线状态\",\n          \"finding\": \"响应者的粪便钙卫蛋白水平（炎症标志物）中位数低于非响应者，但组间差异无统计学意义。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0757ddd3362ddc16e521525\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::19e0ec894f1eb5a1184b3d6d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"在波兰人群中，基线肠道微生物组的组成以及饮食等外在因素是否与黑色素瘤患者对抗PD-1治疗的临床反应（响应 vs. 非响应）相关？是否存在人群特异性的微生物标志物？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::863cf7d94bd87e259d9fdeb2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"波兰人群中的转移性黑色素瘤患者（接受抗PD-1治疗）及健康对照，聚焦基线肠道微生物组组成、饮食模式与免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）疗效的关联。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ba74aefc5df7bb8b114ac5d3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本研究旨在探讨波兰裔黑色素瘤患者对抗PD-1治疗的反应与其基线肠道微生物组及外在修饰因素（如饮食）之间的关联。研究招募了64名接受抗PD-1治疗的患者和10名健康对照，通过问卷调查收集人口统计学、生活方式和饮食数据，并在治疗前采集粪便样本进行16S rRNA基因测序（metataxonomics）及部分宏基因组鸟枪法测序。结果显示，响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）在肠道菌群结构上存在显著差异：响应者的拟杆菌门/厚壁菌门（Bacteroidota/Firmicutes）比值较高，物种丰富度较低；响应者肠道中普雷沃氏菌（Prevotella copri）和均匀拟杆菌（Bacteroides uniformis）丰度较高，而非响应者则富集普拉梭菌（Faecalibacterium prausnitzii）、肠脱硫弧菌（Desulfovibrio intestinalis）及部分未分类厚壁菌。此外，高植物摄入和低乳制品摄入与更好的治疗反应相关。该研究强调了肠道微生物组和饮食对ICI疗效的影响具有人群特异性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::efd525b8d51c8646673bf5ad\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅限波兰人群，不能直接外推至其他种族或地理区域；观察性关联，非因果证明。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了波兰人群中与抗PD-1治疗响应正相关的特定微生物类群（P. copri, B. uniformis）和负相关类群（F. prausnitzii, D. intestinalis）的具体数据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::825c7f4f98b5e07f9c30a0ec\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"基于自我报告问卷，缺乏对具体营养成分或代谢产物的直接测量；混杂因素（如整体生活方式）未完全控制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了饮食模式（高植物摄入、低乳制品摄入）与ICI治疗响应相关的流行病学证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::924f3d1141577180ee5bcbb0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"钙卫蛋白差异无统计学意义；未直接测定免疫细胞浸润或细胞因子水平；机制链条不完整。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"探讨了肠道菌群组成与宿主肠道炎症状态（通过粪便钙卫蛋白衡量）的潜在联系，尽管统计上不显著，但趋势显示响应者炎症水平较低。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0ab239de79b2493b354259b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"作者指出与其他队列（如中国NSCLC患者中P. copri有益，或某些黑色素瘤队列中Faecalibacterium有益）结果的矛盾，强调单一物种不能作为跨人群的通用生物标志物。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e01134b66ca5c18493345af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究发现高植物摄入和低乳制品摄入与良好预后相关，并引用文献说明膳食纤维可能通过产生短链脂肪酸（SCFAs）增强T细胞反应。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b9ee09f7293357ceedf2c7af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究的发现基于波兰特定人群，其微生物组特征受当地饮食和文化影响，结果不能直接推广到其他种族或地区。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::089fc94ec405841194913163\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"对照组年龄显著小于患者组，且样本量小，这可能影响基线微生物组比较的解释力，需谨慎对待与健康对照的比较结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c90a11b11848cab5e8c2f7f7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"饮食数据来自问卷，存在主观性和回忆偏差，且未量化具体营养素摄入量，仅能反映大致饮食模式。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::854f2417fb331859fb4ff475\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"虽然发现了微生物与响应的关联，但未阐明具体的分子机制（如代谢产物、抗原模拟等），因此不能用于解释确切的生物学通路。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::55c6fd10a6749abc57a112b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0545\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"pdf\",\n              \"reason\": \"full-page text extracted; page positions retained\",\n              \"status\": \"fitz\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"fitz\",\n              \"reason\": \"layout, table relations, formulas, figure pixels, and scanned text may be lost\",\n              \"status\": \"known_gap\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::1bb80f168552ffb9a6448494\",\n          \"snapshot::f8979429b0413510bd6a75a4\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::661ac39e317c4d00a2d636c4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4dd74fbdc2f421ab931a4cb0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::711d27360533c41d6d2ec36c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用范围综述方法论。使用PICO框架构建指导问题，在PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, Scopus, SciELO, LILACS五个数据库进行结构化搜索。纳入标准为涉及成年癌症患者、接受系统性肿瘤治疗、进行肠道微生物组分析并明确链接到治疗反应/毒性/预后的研究。排除儿科、仅放疗/手术、纯体外实验及2015年前文献。数据提取通过标准化表格进行，涵盖研究设计、人群特征、微生物分析方法、预测模型性能及主要结果。最终通过叙事综合法（narrative synthesis）对数据进行定性汇总，按癌症类型和治疗模式分类，重点区分“定量预测模型”与“微生物特征描述”，并识别知识空白和方法学局限。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::011d8e1b72c422e144efa713\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了2015-2025年间肠道微生物组在肿瘤治疗反应中应用的全面地图，区分了预测模型开发与微生物特征描述两类证据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为范围综述，不进行质量评估或因果推断；未提供定量荟萃分析结果；所引用的原始研究多为小样本或回顾性，存在选择偏倚和混杂因素控制不足的风险。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47aa59edf8e80e7879afe702\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了微生物组预测模型在特定情境下（如尿路上皮癌、直肠癌）超越传统临床标记物的潜力，强调了菌株水平分辨率的重要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"不同研究的测序技术、生信流程和统计方法高度异质，导致直接比较困难；多数证据仍为关联性而非因果性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7ee2bfeae4e357feca73e50\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"指出了临床转化的主要障碍：方法学标准化缺失、外部验证不足、机制不明及监管挑战。\",\n          \"limits\": \"未能提供具体的标准化协议建议或成本效益分析的详细数据；对真菌、病毒等非细菌微生物的作用探讨有限。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::83d1af535bb6a4c8baae2ee9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）治疗，多中心队列及荟萃分析\",\n          \"finding\": \"菌株水平的微生物特征比临床因素更具预测力。Gunjur等(2024)发现针对联合ICI反应的菌株特征AUC为0.73，优于临床因素的0.56；但泛癌种通用特征在不同ICI方案间外推性较差（一致方案AUC 0.65 vs 不一致方案0.51）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::aa01327d182b7a35bd738a5f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"新辅助化疗，尿路上皮癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"微生物组预测模型表现优于临床变量。Bukavina等(2024)开发的随机森林模型预测完全缓解（CR）的AUC为0.88，而临床因素仅为0.50；高拟杆菌属丰度与较差反应相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::65ce34ec16ea84186df5a999\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"同步放化疗，鼻咽癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"益生菌干预可降低毒性。Xia等(2021)的II期试验显示，益生菌鸡尾酒将3-4级口腔粘膜炎发生率从47.1%降至25%，并通过调节肠道菌群失调和增强免疫反应发挥作用。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fdaca457d135841bbe395399\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"新辅助免疫放化疗，局部晚期直肠癌\",\n          \"finding\": \"物种水平模型具有高预测准确性。Yang等(2024)开发的SPEED模型在训练集AUC为98.8%，验证集为77.8%，用于预测病理完全缓解（pCR）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cb0b5abe6bd93e8ca5e5c6b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"多种实体瘤，综述综合\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定菌属与疗效/毒性关联。双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等通常与ICI良好反应相关；梭杆菌、拟杆菌等在部分研究中与化疗耐药或毒性增加相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39bf57bd7ec01753d11856ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e3b08f72d596718e9bb782c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组衍生的生物标志物和预测模型在肿瘤治疗反应实践中具有何种临床潜力？具体动机在于应对癌症治疗的异质性响应、固有毒性及耐药性挑战，寻找能实现更精准患者选择和疗法优化的新型生物标志物。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c91c85e8effd4baf32727a9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"成人癌症患者（涵盖结直肠癌、黑色素瘤、非小细胞肺癌、食管癌、尿路上皮癌等实体瘤），接受全身性肿瘤治疗（化疗、免疫检查点抑制剂ICIs、靶向治疗及联合方案）。研究范围聚焦于肠道微生物组作为生物标志物在预测治疗反应、毒性及疾病进程中的临床潜力，包括微生物特征识别和预测模型的开发/验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::738eff2017d024fc1b01f364\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇遵循JBI指南和PRISMA-ScR报告的范围综述（scoping review），旨在系统映射并批判性地描述当前关于肠道微生物组在肿瘤学中作为生物标志物的证据。作者检索了2015年至2025年间发表的20项相关研究，涵盖了观察性队列、临床试验和机制研究。综述重点分析了特定微生物类群如何影响免疫治疗和化疗的疗效，以及它们对治疗相关毒性的调节作用。研究发现，基于微生物组的预测模型在某些情况下优于传统临床标记物（如尿路上皮癌中AUC达0.88 vs 0.50），且特定干预（如益生菌）可减轻毒性。然而，综述也指出，由于方法学异质性、缺乏外部验证和机制理解不完整，这些模型的临床转化仍面临挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85d4c075f44e0f132e06caed\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"预测模型的性能数据来自特定队列，外推性受限；FMT试验样本量小（n=15）；大多数关联证据来自观察性研究，不能直接证明因果关系。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICI疗效的具体微生物特征和预测模型性能数据。包括：1) Gunjur等(2024)的多中心研究显示菌株水平特征对联合ICI反应的预测能力（AUC 0.73）优于临床因素；2) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Gopalakrishnan等(2018)综述指出的与良好ICI反应相关的菌属（双歧杆菌、阿克曼氏菌、粪杆菌等）；3) Davar等(2021)的临床试验显示FMT可使PD-1难治性黑色素瘤患者获得客观缓解（20%）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::09a6b7bfdf51f2fbcab58d48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该综述主要归纳其他研究的机制发现，本身未提供新的机制实验数据；许多机制仍处于假说阶段，需结合原文献进一步验证；未详细阐述所有可能的代谢途径。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了微生物组调节ICI疗效的可能机制线索和间接证据。包括：1) Gazzaniga & Kasper (2025)和Chrysostomou等(2023)综述提到的免疫调节机制（如激活T细胞、NK细胞、I型干扰素通路）；2) McCulloch等(2022)观察到不利微生物特征与全身炎症（NLR升高）相关；3) Davar等(2021)发现FMT诱导CD8+ T细胞活化；4) 综述指出抗生素使用可能削弱ICI疗效，暗示生态依赖性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::17e85bdc44e67b65e568505b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述指出当前证据的方法学异质性（样本采集、DNA提取、生信流程）、缺乏外部验证、小样本量导致的过拟合风险，以及因果关系的缺失。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2d2018252fd4aee42531eb16\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述提到微生物组也影响化疗疗效（如梭杆菌促进耐药，拟杆菌改善某些化疗药效果）和毒性（如益生菌降低粘膜炎，特定菌属预测3-4级毒性）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93842ba0acb7c1623cffc35d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"综述提到微生物组特征在早期检测（结直肠腺瘤/癌，AUC 96%/87%）和疾病进展预测（如mCRC中乳酸杆菌与反应相关）中的潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::92203afa91a5d08ad9c31eae\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述是范围综述，其结论基于对20项研究的叙事综合，而非定量荟萃分析。因此，其提供的“AUC”等性能指标应视为各独立研究的结果汇总，而非经过严格统计合并的估计值。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f144188f88dd66e6b5199a8c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述中引用的机制解释（如免疫激活、代谢产物作用）主要来自被综述的原始文献或评论文章，并非本综述作者的新发现。在引用时需明确来源。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2bdb542a3b579fd596759670\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述强调“菌株水平”特征的重要性，但这主要基于Gunjur等(2024)的一项研究，其他多数研究停留在属或种水平。因此，菌株水平的优越性尚需更多证据支持。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2fa1a7af600d3f8db94c74b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述包含了一些非ICI治疗（如化疗、靶向治疗）的研究，在应用于回答ICI相关问题时，需注意区分不同治疗模式的微生物组相互作用差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f33418f66f54c2ba117b589d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"综述指出临床转化面临巨大挑战，因此在利用其提供的积极发现（如高AUC）时，必须同时强调其探索性质和缺乏外部验证的局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::269a6177926dee975b0abb8c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0026\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::f7716cb6058d5ce6dc7380a5\",\n          \"snapshot::5faffef44afd82f262ce3f13\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3170d76df87bfb377320ebc6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::833ddf71a11d978e6fce42b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bce53def04698b2385f517a0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"As a review article, the approach involves a critical appraisal of published literature rather than primary data generation. The authors systematically discuss: 1) Preclinical models identifying key bacterial species; 2) Clinical correlations between stool microbiome composition and ICI outcomes; 3) The impact of antibiotics on survival; 4) Specific intervention trials for prebiotics (dietary fiber), probiotics (CBM588, SER-401), and FMT across different tumor types and lines of therapy. They compare results against historical benchmarks and note limitations such as small sample sizes and heterogeneity in trial designs.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb889e487c6bdd1e356372eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive synthesis of current evidence linking gut microbiome composition to ICI efficacy in solid tumors, categorizing strategies into prebiotics, probiotics, and FMT.\",\n          \"limits\": \"The field lacks large, definitive randomized trials; most evidence comes from small phase I/II studies or retrospective analyses. The review acknowledges that widespread adoption is premature and mechanisms are not fully elucidated.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b772a2563878345157adfe5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Highlights the complexity of microbial effects, noting that both low and excessively high levels of certain bacteria (e.g., Akkermansia) may be suboptimal, suggesting a need for balanced composition rather than single-species enrichment.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Does not provide causal mechanistic proof for all observed associations; many findings are correlative.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d8a1dbcd8a5f17abeac1cf9e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific ongoing trials and future directions, such as stratification based on baseline microbiome composition.\",\n          \"limits\": \"Cannot predict the success of future trials or resolve uncertainties regarding universal vs. personalized application of microbiome therapies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6a77b53a16f1542d379f2044\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Preclinical and observational clinical studies\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific bacterial taxa (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) correlate with favorable responses to anti-PD-1 antibodies, while antibiotic use before/during ICI initiation is associated with higher primary resistance and shorter overall survival.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0ee1f89ce9752d4834de52d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical trials of Probiotics (CBM588)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Small prospective trials in mRCC showed significantly improved progression-free survival and overall response rates when CBM588 was added to ICI-based regimens, though sample sizes were limited (n=30 per arm).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c04267c3ab6c013d3e805b57\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Clinical trials of FMT\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT combined with ICIs showed encouraging results in refractory melanoma (ORR 30%) and frontline settings for melanoma (ORR 65%), NSCLC (ORR 77%), and RCC (12-month PFS improved from 35% to 67%). However, benefits were not consistent in all contexts, such as microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer where outcomes were comparable to historical controls without FMT.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0fbe205ee9cf1e2729d24317\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Biomarker development\",\n          \"finding\": \"The TOPOSCORE biomarker, integrating Akkermansia with other microbial groups, showed significant correlation with overall survival in cohorts of mNSCLC, mRCC, and urothelial carcinoma.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c47c382f8fcd311029400a6b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::391636a4ef531dc3e03166fa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The paper addresses the growing interest in microbiome modulation as a therapeutic strategy to overcome resistance to ICIs in oncology. It seeks to summarize current evidence regarding which microbial species are beneficial or detrimental, how disruption affects outcomes, and whether specific modulation strategies (prebiotics, probiotics, FMT) show clinical benefit.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d466f3497f07b41883777b89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interplay between the gut microbiome and immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs) in patients with solid malignancies, specifically advanced melanoma, metastatic renal cell carcinoma (mRCC), and metastatic non–small cell lung cancer (mNSCLC). It covers preclinical evidence, clinical observations of microbial associations, and various modulation strategies including prebiotics, probiotics, and fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8bf43a9c720757c7c1b29667\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This article is a narrative review that critically appraises existing studies on how gut microbiome modulation can enhance the efficacy of ICIs in solid tumors. It synthesizes preclinical findings linking specific bacterial taxa to treatment response, discusses the negative impact of antibiotic-induced dysbiosis, and evaluates clinical data from trials involving dietary interventions, probiotic supplementation, and FMT. The authors highlight promising signals but emphasize the lack of large-scale randomized controlled trials needed to establish standard of care.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::067e4c00a3d6d84463a180d1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Most clinical data are from small, non-randomized, or early-phase trials. Cannot definitively prove causality for all associations. The review itself notes that large RCTs are lacking.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Summarizes clinical evidence showing that specific gut microbes (Ruminococcaceae, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) are associated with improved ICI outcomes, while antibiotic disruption correlates with poorer survival. Provides ORR and PFS data from FMT and probiotic trials in melanoma, RCC, and NSCLC.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2cbbb1c1818351f5263e174a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"The review is descriptive and does not present new mechanistic experiments. Mechanisms are largely inferred from preclinical models or translational analyses of small cohorts. Does not provide detailed molecular pathway analysis.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Discusses potential mechanisms indirectly through observed effects: e.g., dietary fiber enhancing postbiotic production, vancomycin preconditioning disrupting immunity, and intratumoral Gammaproteobacteria hindering gemcitabine response. Mentions the role of short-chain fatty acids.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::193d9a5f14c622a00b8fa4ba\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"The review establishes the rationale for microbiome modulation, citing preclinical discoveries (Sivan et al., Vétizou et al.) and the general interplay between gut microbiome and immunity.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::442c140f14f35073e88fda05\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Contrasting results: FMT worked well in melanoma/RCC/NSCLC but showed no added benefit over historical controls in microsatellite-stable colorectal cancer.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::53f032c1944a751907a8ef5a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of small sample sizes, lack of standardization in FMT donors (responders vs. healthy volunteers), and conflicting data on single-biomarker utility (Akkermansia levels).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9e457f01ec0c174b1c1a5c20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative summary, not a systematic meta-analysis. Do not treat its conclusions as definitive consensus.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2f55750dba533f27c47b404c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Clinical trial results cited are primarily from Phase I/II studies with small sample sizes; avoid overstating efficacy as established fact.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b246c5f5e588d398b2174b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Mechanistic claims are largely based on preclinical models or correlational clinical data; distinguish between observed association and proven mechanism.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::895c49a50d8426f8ea373423\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review explicitly states that large randomized trials are lacking; do not imply that these strategies are standard of care.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b149a9f56e3601f28672e249\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0215\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::05df8fdca8777120f8d54673\",\n          \"snapshot::78c448ac93100acb4520a4dd\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8e24c98ddc10d25e6368e25c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c7751d6078705a8eed77bd20\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b7b7e3472b4df79f76e0d24c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙述性综述方法，综合了机制研究（前临床模型与人类观察数据）和临床干预试验证据。具体路线包括：1）梳理微生物组影响ICI的药理学基础（抗原呈递、代谢物耦合、屏障完整性）；2）分类评估三类主要干预手段（FMT、LBPs、定义菌群）的代表性临床试验结果；3）讨论影响可重复性的转化因素（共用药、饮食、定植率）及安全监管问题。未进行系统检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于现有文献进行逻辑整合与批判性评议。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d823b853e4ac54a493eee6ef\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于微生物组工程化干预ICI治疗的最新临床证据综合，特别区分了FMT、LBPs和定义菌群三种模态的优缺点及适用场景。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为迷你综述，未提供新的原始实验数据；对特定菌株或代谢物的因果机制多基于前临床模型或间接人类证据，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的确证数据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::cdc0eb48bfb3cc26a577a419\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了将微生物组干预视为“生态药理学”而非简单附加剂的框架，强调了基线生态、共用药和功能性读出（如代谢物、定植率）的重要性。\",\n          \"limits\": \"对于不同肿瘤类型间微生物组效应的异质性解释有限，主要依赖已发表的小规模试验，难以推断普适性规律。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c698a9fd6f94a8050dbc3115\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了安全与监管优先事项，包括供体筛查、追溯性及报告标准，为未来临床试验设计提供了实用指南。\",\n          \"limits\": \"监管建议基于现有案例和专家共识，尚未形成统一的行业标准，具体实施细节尚待后续研究明确。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::698814d6ffd5131ce300e4d6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"抗PD-1难治性转移性黑色素瘤\",\n          \"finding\": \"来自反应者的粪菌移植（FMT）提供了最强的人类概念验证，部分患者实现了临床再敏感化，并伴随供体型微生物特征和肿瘤免疫重塑。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8fa931de280fc236eee06476\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用活体生物制剂（如CBM588）联合ICI\",\n          \"finding\": \"在肾细胞癌中显示出改善临床结果的探索性信号，且能显著改变粪便微生物组特征，但结果具有情境依赖性，需更多大样本验证。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ccc398d5ad7381abec37394\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"使用定义菌群（如SER-401）及抗生素预处理\",\n          \"finding\": \"一项针对黑色素瘤的Ib期试验因入组不足未能得出效力结论，但揭示了广谱抗生素预处理可能破坏保护性免疫准备，提示“清除后添加”策略存在设计陷阱。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46a823fe6dc2d69e904ef7b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"ICI相关的难治性结肠炎\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT在病例系列和转化研究中显示出修复生态平衡、恢复黏膜免疫耐受的活动，支持其作为毒性管理的潜在手段。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7235049ddd5daa54ae6a8121\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1fc6d62ba3897e0fe7ee791b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管ICIs改变了多种恶性肿瘤的管理方式，但仅对部分患者有效且伴随毒性。现有的组织生物标志物无法完全捕捉宿主层面的决定因素。本研究试图解决的核心问题是：肠道微生物组如何作为可操作的调节器影响ICI的敏感性和毒性？以及目前基于微生物组的临床干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）的证据基础和转化障碍是什么？\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0de486040443081d8ed9cbc1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"聚焦于实体瘤（特别是黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、非小细胞肺癌等）患者接受免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs，如抗PD-1/CTLA-4治疗）时的疗效与毒性管理。研究对象为肠道微生物组及其工程化干预策略，涵盖从基础机制到临床转化试验的综合分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::08bc0ccb88530457d6c7da11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇迷你综述，旨在将微生物生态学原理与抗原呈递、T细胞启动及代谢物信号传导等生物学机制联系起来，并系统总结了三种主要干预模式（粪菌移植FMT、活体生物制剂LBPs、定义菌群Consortia）的临床证据。文章指出，肠道微生物组不仅是预测标志物，更是可操作的宿主水平调节剂，能够同时影响抗肿瘤疗效和免疫相关不良事件（irAEs）。通过回顾早期临床试验，作者强调了微生物组干预在重新敏感化难治性肿瘤中的概念验证价值，同时也指出了当前干预措施在可重复性、安全性及标准化方面的挑战。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c38bcef62c8079a6036e37c8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"证据主要来自小规模Phase 1/Ib期试验，样本量小，异质性高。不能直接外推至所有一线治疗场景或所有肿瘤类型。特别是SER-401试验未达效力终点，需谨慎解读。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了三类主要微生物组干预策略（FMT、LBPs、Consortia）在实体瘤中的具体临床证据对比。例如，FMT在难治性黑色素瘤中显示出的概念验证效力，以及LBPs在肾细胞癌中的探索性信号。同时指出了定义菌群试验中因抗生素预处理导致的负面设计教训。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0e83796c6787bdce34f2f296\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"许多机制细节源自前临床模型（小鼠），人类证据多为间接支持（如FMT后的免疫重塑观察）。代谢物水平的因果关系在人类中尚未完全确立，需注意区分观察性关联与因果证据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物组影响ICI疗效的生物学机制框架，包括：1）通过促进树突状细胞激活和交叉呈递来增强CD8+ T细胞反应；2）通过短链脂肪酸等代谢物调节先天免疫编程和炎症基调；3）通过维持肠道屏障完整性来减少系统性炎症和irAEs风险。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d86b2c26e65d14b0a2de91e0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"讨论了基线生态、共用药（抗生素、PPI、激素）、饮食和定植率对干预结果的影响。强调了‘生态药理学’概念，即干预不是简单的药物添加，而是生态扰动。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8449be79b3a7045e41c5dacb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到了耐药大肠杆菌血症、产志贺毒素大肠杆菌以及SARS-CoV-2传播的案例，强调了供体筛查和制造控制的重要性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5c4718a22ebccf62e6d86dfd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文主要关注实体瘤（黑色素瘤、肾细胞癌、NSCLC），其结论不一定适用于血液肿瘤或其他癌症类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::434f935a5128024bbc9228db\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的‘强概念验证’仅限于抗PD-1难治性黑色素瘤中的FMT，不应过度推广到其他干预模式或肿瘤类型。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::736f594938f6aedd75c4d1dd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分混合了前临床模型和人类观察数据，需明确区分哪些是已证实的人类因果机制，哪些是基于模型的推测。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b0fe5dc8f31ddf0d2f44a79a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床试验结果多为早期阶段（Phase 1/Ib），效力结论往往受限（如SER-401试验），解读时需强调其探索性质。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e325d70a97f845ed6b9630a4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0178\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::092a7ef81b878efa4c53c58a\",\n          \"snapshot::2cc8835fd55ad20a54b20c10\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9ffb961f33f663bbe3d8758c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"structured_partial\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::39e0ed7f8bbe7249a0cc470d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d1619fdda7516b77df89edca\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用叙事性综述方法，综合了来自临床前研究（动物模型、体外实验）和临床研究（人类队列、病例报告、准实验研究）的证据。作者并未进行系统性的文献检索或定量荟萃分析，而是基于已有文献对微生物组组成、代谢产物、免疫细胞互作以及各类干预手段的效果进行定性描述和机制解释。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c52075ce0089f1f796870060\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统梳理了肠道微生物组影响CRC免疫治疗响应的多种机制路径（包括代谢物、免疫细胞招募、屏障功能等），并汇总了益生菌、FMT、饮食及中药等多种干预手段的临床前和部分临床证据。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为叙事性综述，未进行系统性文献检索或偏倚风险评估；结论受限于所引用研究的异质性（样本量小、设计多样）；部分发现（如A. muciniphila的作用）存在矛盾；缺乏对干预措施直接比较的定量证据；安全性讨论主要基于个案或小规模试验，尚不足以确立常规临床应用的规范。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::84c41d1446ea2fd02ca22186\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"MSS/pMMR CRC模型及临床背景\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定微生物群（如Akkermansia muciniphila, Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus等）及其代谢产物（如短链脂肪酸SCFAs）可通过促进CD8+ T细胞浸润、抑制调节性T细胞（Tregs）和髓源性抑制细胞（MDSCs），增强抗PD-1/PD-L1疗法的疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0bb6354b1ffa085e58316dd9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"不同菌株作用\",\n          \"finding\": \"部分病原体（如Fusobacterium nucleatum, Porphyromonas gingivalis）通过诱导免疫抑制微环境降低ICIs疗效；而某些益生菌株（如L. paracasei sh2020）可增强抗CTLA-4疗法效果。A. muciniphila的作用存在争议，既有促癌报道也有抑癌报道，但与C. butyricum联用可协同增强疗效。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eeec402edb49ca9e42b9e1d0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT临床应用\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT联合ICIs在MSS转移性CRC的II期临床试验（RENMIN-215）中显示出改善生存率和可控的安全性，外周γδ2 T细胞水平升高与响应相关。但FMT存在供体筛选困难、耐药基因转移及感染风险等安全顾虑。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::85a176f85847c29434a827f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"其他干预手段\",\n          \"finding\": \"中药复方（如清解胶囊、葛根芩连汤）和膳食纤维饮食可调节菌群结构，增加有益菌丰度，抑制肿瘤生长；工程化益生菌和纳米技术递送系统展示了克服免疫耐药的潜力。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c8766415c71f1b0aa83a51c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::82c1049c351f6660caa30818\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"解决ICIs在大多数结直肠癌患者（尤其是MSS/pMMR型）中疗效有限的问题，探索如何通过调节肠道微生物组来克服免疫治疗耐药性，并识别相关的安全隐患。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::edd6329a6caa52f247dce0af\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"结直肠癌（CRC）患者，特别是微卫星稳定/错配修复 proficient (MSS/pMMR) 亚型；聚焦肠道微生物组对免疫检查点抑制剂（ICIs）疗效的影响及基于微生物组的干预策略。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3e4a05237cb42d6954c814b0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇叙事性综述，旨在总结肠道微生物组在结直肠癌发生、发展及免疫治疗反应中的作用机制，并评估益生菌、粪菌移植（FMT）、饮食调节和传统药物等微生物组干预措施作为ICIs辅助治疗的潜力与安全性。文章指出，尽管微生物组调控在临床前模型中显示出增强抗肿瘤免疫的潜力，但现有证据存在不一致性且缺乏大规模临床试验支持，因此强调需要标准化的方法和更严谨的临床验证。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ebd11b917309870a1c077e6e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"证据主要来自小鼠模型和小规模人类研究，缺乏大规模随机对照试验的直接因果证明；不同研究间结果存在冲突（如A. muciniphila）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了肠道微生物组影响ICIs疗效的具体微生物物种（如Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium, Lactobacillus, Fusobacterium）及其在MSS/pMMR CRC中的临床前和初步临床证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5a7b7c989be4d1458c33014d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"多数机制细节源自动物模型或体外实验，在人体内的确切适用性需结合具体临床数据验证；不同机制可能在不同患者亚群中主导作用不同。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"详细阐述了微生物组调节免疫反应的机制，包括：1) 代谢物介导（SCFAs, 4-HPA, 胆汁酸）；2) 免疫细胞招募与极化（CD8+ T cells, DCs, M1/M2 macrophages）；3) 炎症通路激活（TLR4, NF-κB）；4) 屏障功能维持。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9f19d718b8beb25ba0a72627\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"临床证据等级参差不齐，多为II期试验、病例报告或准实验研究；缺乏长期安全性和标准化方案的数据。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"总结了非抗生素类微生物组干预策略（益生菌、FMT、饮食、中药）在增强ICIs疗效方面的潜在应用和现状。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::84acd6806e0eec333e74652d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"MSS/pMMR CRC对ICIs天然耐药的特征，以及肠道微生物组作为关键影响因素的背景介绍。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e018458bdb969bec348e179c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"肿瘤微环境中微生物生态位（microniches）的概念，以及微生物-宿主-免疫系统三角关系的图示化描述。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ae3f21e24e49d1344657963\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Akkermansia muciniphila在CRC中既被报道促癌又被报道抑癌的矛盾发现。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::64c10cff9d71226f6df3ca15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"FMT在临床应用中面临的供体筛选、耐药基因转移和感染风险等安全挑战。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::264cce889a5056e1b23ca71b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是叙事性综述，非系统性综述，其结论反映作者对现有文献的选择性解读，可能存在发表偏倚或选择偏倚。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::43b95aac20cf5e0952d064de\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中引用的许多机制证据来自动物模型（小鼠），不能直接外推至人类患者的全部生理病理过程。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bc41e0e7d6ac4add9ec6afd1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"关于特定益生菌株（如A. muciniphila）的作用存在相互矛盾的文献，需谨慎对待单一方向的概括。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b4fcee3819520eb2e476d1c2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"临床干预效果多基于小规模研究或观察性数据，尚未形成标准治疗方案，不应视为已证实的常规临床指南。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::755083fdbe007a675d60e15b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0439\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_not_scholarly_body\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"known_losses\": [\n                \"headings/tables/math/image pixels are not preserved by this plain HTML projection\"\n              ],\n              \"reason\": \"body converted to structured material; headings/tables/math/image pixels may be lost\",\n              \"status\": \"derived\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"html\",\n              \"reason\": \"html_not_scholarly_body\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"structured_partial\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::00ae381a8034efc1a09ecfba\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::47320b778a94a3f6e1bba0ee\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5b9018b036f8b7172a084833\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eab85e6bee9c4b2fed5a5534\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e2c9835b96f8fc6dc09ac52b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f4f27ebf49eb4765b4072a3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a1803946bf15951d555dd21c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0698d1c77cb0d200e790e2f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n          \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::633e7982644fd55dc1491f2b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7401efb4116390e74b3c0d15\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n          \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4c101d96abe914328c6abdc\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5e3f0657dbc810fb682a25e8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f3675d08d336269e9d5f7b86\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1bc1f290c28d78622ffb8469\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e4fe0aec77d9cea7ccfbcb3b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bee8d56ffb923bd61271c4b9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2653a9eca08d3e9b4aabdd40\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6f7f1819fb2b6498ee2e73b4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::246f46b2e4daa7c0826508a1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::01a4eaf6f9130e6df88a4449\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c302f1d1ebc15fb248ecf95b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::297962d07c0123503e761a0c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4677960f83a51b4866588b1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n          \"evidence\": [],\n          \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n          \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n          \"limitations\": [],\n          \"material_ready\": true,\n          \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n          \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n          \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n          \"status\": \"unmet\",\n          \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::368f88790e7cd7be69d3482e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"supplement_materials\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"auxiliary_material\": \"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\",\n            \"evidence\": [],\n            \"gap_id\": \"case_E_phase3_rct\",\n            \"judgment_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\",\n            \"limitations\": [],\n            \"material_ready\": true,\n            \"material_usefulness\": \"supporting\",\n            \"outline_action_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"remaining_gap\": \"The gap question asks for a completed large randomised phase III trial of a microbiome intervention in cancer patients receiving ICIs. This study is a narrative review and does not report any completed Phase III trials. It explicitly states that 'substantial hurdles remain' and calls for 'large-scale, multicenter, standardized, longitudinal studies,' indicating that such trials were not completed or reported at the time of writing. Therefore, the success criterion of identifying a completed large Phase III trial is not met.\",\n            \"remaining_gap_recovered_by_policy\": false,\n            \"status\": \"unmet\",\n            \"useful_material\": \"The study is a narrative review that synthesizes evidence from preclinical models and early-phase clinical trials (Phase I/II) regarding microbiome interventions in cancer patients receiving immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It details mechanisms by which specific taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Akkermansia, Bifidobacterium) and metabolites (SCFAs, indoles, TMAO) modulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed. It highlights significant heterogeneity in study cohorts and methodologies, preventing the establishment of reproducible predictive models or definitive clinical intervention strategies.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d402e4e4dd606e12c0dadf8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-0c71639dc3330990d568\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2c047b67f79872fa4042\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-2d4faf2da7bc361a24e6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::3d8858e15482badd0b239265\",\n          \"snapshot::ffb9e07e822a6a49bf255cf0\",\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\",\n          \"snapshot::b864e5d6aff2b761a52deb5b\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::782ec3f7244d0ab076658c3c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science Core Collection, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the effects of gut microbiota or metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction was guided by STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: first covering ICI mechanisms, then the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, followed by specific metabolite classes, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and finally microbiome-based interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d7e9648a9d3a228b80acd4f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut microbes and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, categorizing interventions by their molecular targets (STING, NOD2, AhR, etc.).\",\n          \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review acknowledges significant methodological heterogeneity across studies and notes that many proposed biomarkers and interventions require validation in large-scale, standardized longitudinal studies.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6e33ef85bc9029ac9138418\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Melanoma patients treated with anti-CTLA-4 (ipilimumab)\",\n          \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (e.g., B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for antitumor efficacy.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::69bf00aad7ea27d8d011a5f9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"NSCLC patients treated with anti-PD-1\",\n          \"finding\": \"High relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila (Akk-high) was associated with worse overall survival compared to Akk-low groups, challenging the binary 'good vs bad' bacteria concept and highlighting cohort/cancer-type dependency.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d3b8e49c5165f6a25f200eab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens\",\n          \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent; different ICIs rely on distinct microbial signatures (e.g., Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1 vs. Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4).\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5a2ef1b4e9581d3a710c521\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Tryptophan metabolites (3-IAld, IPA)\",\n          \"finding\": \"3-IAld alleviates colitis and enhances efficacy via AhR/IL-22; IPA provides cardioprotection via AhR/PI3K/AKT signaling.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::361feac329a052a7d78f53b7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"SCFAs (Butyrate, Propionate, Acetate)\",\n          \"finding\": \"Butyrate protects against cardiotoxicity via PPARa-CYP4X1 and enhances antigen presentation via HDAC inhibition; Propionate/Acetate promote Treg homeostasis and memory CD8+ T-cell differentiation.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::120f673d74db8c5732a0396e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"TMAO\",\n          \"finding\": \"Triggers immunogenic tumor cell death (pyroptosis) via PERK-GSDME pathway, recruiting CD8+ T cells.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b3cf17eff823e01454721f6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"Probiotics (LGG, BF839, Akk)\",\n          \"finding\": \"LGG and BF839 activate cGAS-STING axis in dendritic cells to enhance CD8+ T cell infiltration; Akk produces c-di-AMP which directly activates STING.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0b0761c9932abc9ab5a5874d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"FMT interventions\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT from long-term responders to PD-1 therapy showed higher efficacy than healthy donors; response correlated with loss of deleterious baseline species rather than just engraftment of donor strains.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6c7424e735d637988d2eced9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The clinical utility of ICIs is limited by interpatient variability in efficacy and the occurrence of systemic toxicities (irAEs). The review aims to systematically delineate the microbiome-metabolite-immune axis to understand these variations and optimize the balance between therapeutic gain and toxicity, ultimately guiding the development of precise microbial interventions.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b70d300ebe4f7a632702a5f0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review focuses on the gut microbiome and its metabolic byproducts as systemic regulators of immune function, specifically in the context of cancer immunotherapy using immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs). It covers mechanisms of ICI action (PD-1/PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, TIM-3), the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions across different cancer types and cohorts, microbial metabolites (tryptophan derivatives, SCFAs, TMAO, inosine, bile acids, polyamines) as mediators of efficacy and toxicity, and microbiome-based interventions including probiotics, FMT, postbiotics, and dietary fiber.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e3b528b07174c7f2c4e9b9b5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and microbe-derived metabolites regulate the efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs) of ICIs. It highlights specific taxa like Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, and Akkermansia muciniphila that potentiate therapeutic responses via pathways such as cGAS-STING and NOD2. The review also details how microbial metabolites protect organs like the heart and colon from inflammation while enhancing anti-tumor immunity. It evaluates emerging interventions like FMT and next-generation probiotics, noting that while preclinical and Phase I trials show feasibility, substantial hurdles remain regarding cohort heterogeneity, methodological standardization, and the need for large-scale longitudinal studies to establish reproducible predictive models.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7a16470a938828a019a65473\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Critiques the reliance on single-taxa abundance, advocates for topology-based approaches, and highlights logistical barriers like metagenomic turnaround times for precision nutrition.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bf0ea10d71d03a741315fcbb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"Describes FMT from responders vs. healthy donors, encapsulation technologies for probiotics, and the double-edged nature of antibiotic preconditioning and high-fiber diets.\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cebf65ae6c2fb3a2b3291c3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Findings are based on a synthesis of various studies with differing methodologies; causal relationships are often inferred from preclinical models or observational data rather than definitive clinical trials.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Details the context-dependent nature of microbiome-ICI interactions, showing that beneficial taxa vary by cancer type and ICI regimen (e.g., Bacteroides for CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium for PD-1, variable role of Akk). It also discusses the trade-off between efficacy and toxicity, noting that some microbes protective in one context may be detrimental in another.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d90e74ef12c1e1106eacf6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are described from murine models or in vitro studies; human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are noted as undefined.\",\n          \"contribution\": \"Provides specific molecular mechanisms linking microbes/metabolites to immune modulation. For example, it describes how LGG and BF839 activate the cGAS-STING pathway, how tryptophan metabolites act via AhR, and how SCFAs influence T-cell function and barrier integrity through epigenetic and receptor-mediated pathways.\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::74ec76742b9f6daf3762643e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide quantitative meta-analytic results; effect sizes and statistical significance should not be inferred from this text alone.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::995110f30544c2be6aece91c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models (mice) or small clinical cohorts; extrapolation to broader human populations requires caution.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b16eb73c69f940a7edbd13bf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"The role of specific microbes (e.g., Akkermansia) can be context-dependent and even contradictory across studies; avoid treating any single taxon as universally beneficial or detrimental.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d7b3fab2b1cb1884ae2d02d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"Claims about the efficacy of interventions like FMT or probiotics are primarily based on early-phase trials or preclinical data; robust clinical validation is still needed.\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::de02bcabb5761d1a2aab77da\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"approach\": \"The authors conducted a comprehensive literature search across PubMed/MEDLINE, Web of Science, and Embase up to May 1, 2026. They included original studies, RCTs, cohort studies, and preclinical investigations examining the impact of gut microbiota/metabolites on ICI efficacy or toxicities. Data extraction followed STORMS guidelines. As a narrative review, formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis were not performed. The synthesis is organized thematically: mechanisms of ICIs, heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions, microbial metabolites as mediators, clinical heterogeneity of irAEs, and microbiome-based interventions.\",\n            \"contribution_and_limits\": [\n              {\n                \"contribution\": \"Provides a comprehensive mechanistic synthesis linking specific gut taxa and metabolites to ICI efficacy and irAE mitigation, highlighting context-dependent biomarkers rather than universal signatures.\",\n                \"limits\": \"As a narrative review, it lacks formal risk-of-bias assessment, quality grading, and statistical meta-analysis. Findings are largely derived from preclinical models or small clinical cohorts with limited covariate adjustment. The review does not establish causal relationships for all proposed mechanisms due to observational data dominance.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"key_findings\": [\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-CTLA-4 therapy; Melanoma patients and mouse models\",\n                \"finding\": \"CTLA-4 blockade reshapes the microbiota, favoring Bacteroides species (B. fragilis, B. thetaiotaomicron), which are critical for therapeutic efficacy via Th1 responses and dendritic cell activation.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Metastatic melanoma patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Responders exhibit higher alpha-diversity and enrichment of Faecalibacterium and Ruminococcaceae; however, only a fraction of human taxa successfully colonize murine models.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Anti-PD-1 therapy; Advanced NSCLC patients\",\n                \"finding\": \"Relative abundance of Akkermansia muciniphila is prognostic; low abundance (<4.8%) correlates with superior overall survival compared to high abundance, challenging the binary 'good/bad' bacteria concept.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Various ICI regimens; Preclinical and clinical cohorts\",\n                \"finding\": \"Microbial influence is context-dependent: Firmicutes/Bacteroidetes associations with irAE risk invert across cancer types (protective in melanoma but linked to severe colitis in hepatobiliary malignancies).\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"conditions\": \"Mechanistic pathways; In vivo and in vitro models\",\n                \"finding\": \"Specific microbes enhance efficacy via distinct pathways: LGG and B. fragilis activate cGAS-STING; Enterococcus expresses SagA to activate NOD2; Alistipes finegoldii uses CXCL16-CXCR6 axis. Metabolites like SCFAs and indoles protect against toxicity via AhR/PPARα/NF-κB modulation.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"paper_kind\": \"review\",\n            \"problem_or_question\": \"To systematically characterize the complex interplay between the gut microbiome, its metabolome, and ICI outcomes (efficacy and toxicity), addressing the clinical heterogeneity in patient responses and the lack of reproducible predictive models or intervention strategies.\",\n            \"research_scope\": \"The review focuses on the interaction between the gut microbiome (specific taxa and metabolites) and the efficacy/toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors (ICIs), including PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 targets. It covers preclinical mechanistic studies and early-phase clinical trials across various solid tumors (melanoma, NSCLC, RCC, gastric/colorectal cancer).\",\n            \"work_summary\": \"This narrative review synthesizes current evidence on how the gut microbiota and their metabolic byproducts regulate ICI efficacy and immune-related adverse events (irAEs). It delineates specific microbial taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1431bb03ae021761d8f92368\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B_variants\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": [\n          {\n            \"broader_review_uses\": [\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Sets the stage for why microbiome modulation is a critical area of research in overcoming ICI limitations.\",\n                \"material\": \"Overview of CTLA-4, PD-1/PD-L1, LAG-3, TIGIT, and TIM-3 mechanisms, and the clinical challenge of interpatient heterogeneity and irAEs.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Contextual background on ICI mechanisms and limitations\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Provides evidence on the feasibility and challenges of translating microbiome science into clinical practice, highlighting the gap between preclinical success and clinical implementation.\",\n                \"material\": \"Discussion of FMT trials (responder-derived vs. healthy donors), probiotic encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition strategies.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Evaluation of microbiome-based interventions\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"connection_to_review\": \"Offers a critical perspective on the current state of the field, suggesting areas where future research needs to improve reproducibility and causal inference.\",\n                \"material\": \"Critique of current study heterogeneity, sample processing issues, and the need for standardized multi-omics approaches.\",\n                \"purpose\": \"Methodological considerations and future directions\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"facet_contributions\": [\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Associations are often based on small cohorts or preclinical models. The review explicitly notes that findings are not universally reproducible and depend heavily on study methodology and cohort characteristics.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Identifies specific microbial taxa associated with ICI response across different cancer types and ICI regimens (e.g., Bacteroides for anti-CTLA-4, Faecalibacterium/Ruminococcaceae for anti-PD-1, Akkermansia abundance levels for NSCLC). Highlights that microbial roles are context-dependent and vary by tumor type and host factors.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F1\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Can be used to support arguments about the heterogeneity of microbiome-ICI interactions and the lack of a universal 'good' microbiome signature. Provides specific examples of taxa to discuss in the context of patient stratification.\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"boundaries\": \"Many mechanisms are derived from murine models or in vitro studies. Human concentration thresholds and spatial dynamics within the tumor microenvironment are often undefined. The review cautions that these mechanisms may not directly translate to clinical efficacy without further validation.\",\n                \"contribution\": \"Details molecular mechanisms by which microbes and metabolites modulate immunity: cGAS-STING activation by LGG and B. fragilis; NOD2 activation by Enterococcus; AhR-mediated barrier protection and cardiotoxicity mitigation by indoles and SCFAs; PERK-GSDME pyroptosis induction by TMAO.\",\n                \"facet_id\": \"F2\",\n                \"possible_uses\": \"Provides mechanistic depth for explaining how the gut microbiome influences ICI efficacy and toxicity. Useful for discussing specific signaling pathways (STING, NOD2, AhR, NF-κB) and their role in remodeling the tumor microenvironment and protecting distal organs.\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"scope_interpretation_cautions\": [\n              \"The review emphasizes that microbial biomarkers are highly context-dependent (tumor type, ICI regimen, host genetics). Do not generalize findings from one cancer type (e.g., melanoma) to others (e.g., hepatobiliary) without considering this variability.\",\n              \"Many mechanistic insights are derived from preclinical models. Clinical translation is still in early phases (Phase I/II trials). Avoid overstating the clinical applicability of specific microbial interventions.\",\n              \"The review is a narrative synthesis and does not provide statistical meta-analyses or formal quality assessments. Treat the synthesized evidence as indicative rather than definitive proof of causality.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        ],\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::bd2a31924b2f1b7a5c0db505\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-b5c2e925a4132b88eff6\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-7f937d5566b4c12030ce\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-a96686bee2f7be7a8dd8\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-724817b1ad2fa81c8182\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-ba354d40740f64366cbf\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-403bce67afb0fdb07c1f\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40f0854379f8b3542a576b91\",\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2088384ebad86f83dd115cc2\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::40488f1658ce0a5b0029a527\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::182a456925359bd5e4cb6b24\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0333\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"local_passages\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"external_calls\": 0,\n          \"passages\": [\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The review discusses the feasibility of interventions such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), probiotics, and postbiotics, citing Phase Ib and Phase II trials (e.g., FMT-LUMINate, Glitza et al.) but explicitly notes that large-scale, multicenter, standardized longitudinal studies are needed.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"机制\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\",\n                \"mechanisms mediate effect\",\n                \"ici\",\n                \"i\",\n                \"ii\",\n                \"iii\",\n                \"nsclc\",\n                \"rct\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 120.720283,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"Supplementary question reading\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"directed_content\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"{\\\"auxiliary_material\\\": \\\"The review provides detailed mechanistic pathways for microbial modulation of immunity, including cGAS-STING activation by Lactobacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) and Bacteroides fragilis, NOD2 activation by Enterococcus, and AhR-mediated barrier protection by indole derivatives. It also outlines the context-dependent nature of microbial biomarkers, noting that associations with efficacy or toxicity vary by cancer type (e.g., melanoma vs. hepatobiliary) and ICI regimen. Specific trial data cited include a Phase Ib trial on antibiotic preconditioning (Glitza et al.), a Phase II FMT trial in NSCLC and melanoma (FMT-LUMINate), and a Phase I trial in gastric cancer (Zhang et al.). The authors emphasize that current evidence is constrained by small sample sizes, lack of standardization, and the predominance of preclinical data.\\\", \\\"evidence\\\": [], \\\"gap_id\\\": \\\"case_E_phase3_rct\\\", \\\"judgment_path\\\": \\\"F:\\\\\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\\\\\outputs\\\\\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\\\\\03_external_closure\\\\\\\\runs\\\\\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\\\\\source_units\\\\\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\\\\\FULFILLMENT_JUDGMENT.json\\\", \\\"limitations\\\": [], \\\"material_ready\\\": true, \\\"material_usefulness\\\": \\\"suppor…\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"best_sentence\": \"The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"card_path\": \"F:\\\\OptoMind-Review-2\\\\outputs\\\\progressive_review_plan\\\\20260926_adaptive_retrieval\\\\03_external_closure\\\\runs\\\\case_E_phase3_rct\\\\source_units\\\\SU02_search_candidate_93c14070cc\\\\card\\\\PAPER_READING_CARD.json\",\n              \"doi\": \"10.3389/fimmu.2026.1803970\",\n              \"limits\": [],\n              \"match_terms\": [\n                \"粪菌移植\",\n                \"益生菌\",\n                \"gut microbiome modulate efficacy immune checkpoint inhibitors solid tumours\"\n              ],\n              \"material_depth\": \"fulltext\",\n              \"paper_id\": \"CorpusId:290154100\",\n              \"pool_action\": \"already_in_pool\",\n              \"reading_path\": \"\",\n              \"score\": 17.613751,\n              \"section_path\": [\n                \"general understanding\",\n                \"work summary\"\n              ],\n              \"segment_kind\": \"card_work_summary\",\n              \"source_handle\": \"P0584\",\n              \"text\": \"taxa (e.g., Bacteroides, Bifidobacterium, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. m, Akkermansia) and metabolites (SCFAs, indole derivatives, TMAO) that modulate antitumor immunity and organ protection. The paper also evaluates emerging microbiome-targeted interventions, such as fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT), next-generation probiotics with encapsulation technologies, postbiotics, and precision nutrition, highlighting the context-dependent nature of these interactions and the need for standardized, multi-omics approaches to develop precise microbial interventions.\",\n              \"title\": \"Navigating the gut–metabolite–immune axis: enhancing efficacy and mitigating toxicity of immune checkpoint inhibitors\",\n              \"usable_fields\": [],\n              \"year\": \"2026\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"question\": \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect? 微生物干预策略的临床转化现状 系统评估粪菌移植（FMT）、活体生物药（LBPs）、益生菌及饮食干预在实体瘤 ICI 治疗中的临床试验数据，区分初治与难治人群的疗效差异，明确证据等级（I/II 期 vs III 期），并分析供体选择、安全性及标准化挑战。 涵盖人体临床试验（I-III 期），聚焦实体瘤（黑色素瘤、NSCLC、RCC、CRC 等）。包括 FMT（供体来源、给药途径）、定义菌群（如 CBM588、MRx0518）、益生菌及饮食干预。明确排除纯临床前研究（除非用于解释机制背景）及非 ICI 背景的微生物干预。严格区分观察性关联与干预性因果证据，标注试验设计类型（单臂 vs RCT）及人群特征（初治 vs 经治）。\",\n          \"reading_mode\": \"focused_local_search\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::bb5eb4bfd56825e2ae776a7e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::d2eba37acde2103b14529835\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::04eaac683222de8ca9070df9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::06a06e3788b228f652f2234d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一项前瞻性、跨机构的多中心转化研究。研究对象为接受新辅助治疗的早期乳腺癌、直肠癌或食管癌患者。排除标准包括既往同种异体组织/实体器官移植史及既往接受过抗癌治疗。数据采集包括在新辅助治疗前、完成后以及完成后六个月进行粪便采样。微生物组分析采用16S rRNA测序。病理反应在手术时评估，分为应答者（pCR）和非应答者。主要终点是检验GM多样性与病理反应的关联。探索性分析包括cf-DNA与GM多样性的关联，以及基线cf-DNA与pCR的关联。统计方法计划使用Shannon指数分析Alpha多样性，Jaccard相似性指数计算Beta多样性，并使用PCA和随机森林进行分类和聚类分析。主要终点的关联将通过调整潜在混杂因素的逻辑回归分析进行评估。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4335ab0b84254bb1619de1a5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于在爱尔兰特定医疗体系下开展大型多中心肿瘤-微生物组转化研究的可行性和方法论框架；确立了研究设计和预期分析路线。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代最终的研究结果、GM多样性与pCR之间的具体关联、任何机制解释或统计学显著性结论。由于研究尚未完成，无法评估其实际科学贡献或外部有效性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b6b5d30ce92296b3fd3c4eb\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"研究进行中，仅基于招募可行性验证\",\n          \"finding\": \"证明了在爱尔兰开展此类转化研究的可行性，并优化了筛选和招募流程以提高招募数量。目前已招募14名患者。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::320fb9443b29f631a256d1d4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::41aeb07965852bce86ea4e11\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管已知肠道微生物组可能通过调节免疫通路影响宿主免疫及对免疫检查点抑制剂的反应，但关于GM多样性如何影响胃肠道和乳腺癌新辅助治疗后的病理完全缓解尚不清楚。本研究旨在解决这一知识空白。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff38897831fd6a0ec9f1ff49\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"爱尔兰多中心前瞻性转化研究，针对早期乳腺癌、直肠癌和食管癌患者，在开始新辅助治疗（化疗、免疫治疗或放化疗）前及治疗后不同时间点收集粪便样本。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f72f8d50d6728b9c9231a8ea\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文介绍了一项正在进行的爱尔兰多中心转化研究，旨在探讨基线肠道微生物组（GM）多样性与新辅助治疗后病理完全缓解（pCR）之间的关联。研究假设基线GM多样性更高将导致更好的病理反应。目前招募仍在进行中，已纳入14名患者，预计2025年初得出结果。摘要主要描述了研究设计、可行性验证及初步招募情况，未提供最终的统计分析结果或发现。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c4920cf42f919cbcc228f58e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该研究尚未提供结果，因此不能用于支持或反驳GM多样性对疗效的影响。仅能作为“正在进行的研究”或“研究缺口”的背景提及。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了关于肠道微生物组多样性与实体瘤新辅助治疗反应之间关联的研究背景和待检验假设。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1c4d84fb7c3a7fd7ceb4eed5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"摘要仅提到GM可能通过调节免疫通路影响宿主免疫，但未在本研究中验证具体机制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"未提供具体的机制证据。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c317d477bfa68247450db74d\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"研究设计细节：多中心、前瞻性、爱尔兰人群、16S rRNA测序、Shannon/Jaccard指数、逻辑回归分析。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a2d7c14d865c1772f5c9db60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"摘要明确指出“little is known about how the GM diversity influences complete pathological response”，且研究预计2025年出结果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::05743daab7f9a70950e809cd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该论文仅为研究方案/进展报告，无最终结果。切勿将其假设或计划当作已证实的发现。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::28f4868d4c01ef55c8555742\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究人群限定为爱尔兰早期乳腺癌、直肠癌和食管癌患者，结果外推需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4de22e3bb2306b19cff594fe\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究关注的是“多样性”而非特定菌群组成，这与某些关注特定菌属的研究不同。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2df6782f572a20b2e37854aa\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"新辅助治疗类型多样（化疗、免疫治疗、放化疗），结果可能因治疗方式而异，需区分看待。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a13e11aec07c79c3b5d5ac28\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0045\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b5ffa54698a5c4af1cec136e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a19c959f8a2acc29636f119b\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b89231969a054b4a89c2a48\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c823cde6fd7be8f3503cb7e3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"系统性文献回顾。作者检索了EMBASE、Web of Science、MEDLINE等数据库，关键词包括(gut microbiota OR gut microbiome) AND (cancer OR oncology) AND (paediatric OR children)。文章结构上先介绍一般背景，再分章节讨论致癌机制、全身治疗相互作用、儿科特异性（发病率、治疗诱导的变化、急慢性并发症）、干预措施，最后总结局限性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::304fdc7a467cbc5937eb2a85\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"系统梳理了儿科肿瘤中微生物组研究的现状，特别区分了血液恶性肿瘤和实体瘤的证据差异。\",\n          \"limits\": \"主要基于观察性研究和小型试点研究，缺乏大规模前瞻性试验；无法确立因果关系（是原因还是结果）；实体瘤数据极度匮乏。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::31af98e275ea3928cfba54b1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了微生物组作为预测生物标志物和个性化治疗靶点的潜力。\",\n          \"limits\": \"目前尚无标准化的干预方案（如益生菌、FMT）在儿科肿瘤中的确切疗效和安全性数据，部分干预存在潜在风险（如菌血症）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ff2cfcc604793b53a9d59566\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"成人免疫检查点抑制剂治疗\",\n          \"finding\": \"抗生素使用可能降低免疫治疗反应；Akkermansia muciniphila丰度高的患者预后更好。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e426c7e2e3a8cb7610cfe635\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"儿童急性淋巴细胞白血病(ALL)\",\n          \"finding\": \"诊断时粪便DNA含量较低；双歧杆菌、乳酸杆菌丰度降低；化疗后微生物多样性显著下降，恢复缓慢。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::3b249c424838c10c3f3f76f3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"儿童实体瘤（横纹肌肉瘤）\",\n          \"finding\": \"小样本研究显示，治疗前微生物多样性较低的患者对放化疗反应较好，但结论受限于样本量。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::46682478facb5aaa26af0904\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"化疗副作用\",\n          \"finding\": \"特定菌群（如肠球菌科、链球菌科）的高丰度与中性粒细胞发热、腹泻等急性并发症相关；Faecalibacterium减少可能与长期肥胖和代谢综合征风险相关。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f6196f1a51bb8d17a7355dca\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"review\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9a8c8c84055f2f5ec45e2efd\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"尽管成人研究中微生物组对肿瘤免疫治疗的影响已较明确，但在儿科人群中，由于病例数少和治疗复杂，其具体作用、对疗效的影响机制以及对副作用的贡献仍不清楚。本文旨在梳理现有文献，填补这一知识空白。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::5698c6861547b14b692a5ea1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"儿科肿瘤（特别是急性淋巴细胞白血病和实体瘤）与肠道微生物组的关系，涵盖发病机制、治疗反应及副作用。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fa48e8593af165fb2b6abbf5\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"这是一篇2022年的综述文章，旨在总结肠道微生物组在儿科肿瘤发生和治疗中的最新研究进展。文章首先概述了微生物组的一般生理作用及其通过免疫调节影响癌症的机制，随后重点讨论了儿科特异性，包括分娩方式、喂养方式对微生物组的影响，以及化疗和放疗引起的微生物组变化。研究发现，微生物组的变化与治疗反应和毒性相关，但目前证据多来自成人或小型儿科队列，且因果关系尚不明确。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::16e154198afee70b84b0d829\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"该综述明确指出儿科实体瘤数据极少，且多数关联未证实因果。不能将此视为儿科ICIs疗效的确切机制解释，仅作为假设生成的来源。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了儿科肿瘤中微生物组与治疗反应关联的临床观察数据。例如，指出ALL患者化疗后多样性降低，且某些菌群丰度变化与疗效相关（尽管主要是描述性关联）。同时引用了成人研究中Akkermansia与ICIs疗效正相关的证据，为儿科可能的类似机制提供类比支持。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9bda68f2ddae3b446d9d8f89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这些机制大多基于成人模型或体外研究，儿科特异性验证不足。综述本身未提供新的机制实验数据，而是汇总现有理论。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"概述了微生物组影响治疗的潜在生物学途径，包括：1）细菌酶解药物代谢（如伊立替康）；2）免疫调节（如双歧杆菌促进T细胞反应）；3）屏障损伤导致细菌易位引发炎症。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::28d3e1b6a2d3d74bf0d52e22\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提到儿科病例数少、治疗复杂（联合化疗/放疗/抗生素）、样本收集困难，导致高质量研究稀缺。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::eb54daf7521fc7faadeaef52\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"剖宫产增加ALL风险，母乳喂养降低ALL风险，涉及微生物组建立的关键窗口期。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e496368c2da663bee84e959f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"提及益生菌可能导致造血干细胞移植患儿菌血症，FMT在儿童中的应用尚不成熟。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dde97d1799340db7c2a03104\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该综述主要关注儿科，但其引用的关键机制（如ICIs疗效）多基于成人研究，使用时需明确区分人群差异，避免直接将成人结论套用于儿科。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6253ea41b94d1e85c041082c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文中提到的许多关联（如菌群与毒性）多为观察性结果，不能推断为因果关系。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8d8cc5c422e1531f2b8f99c1\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"对于实体瘤部分，证据非常薄弱，仅有个案或小样本报告，不应过度解读其普遍性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::73000960b882ef64134393a6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0008\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::b9dc603c11ee193c68e27ba9\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::48b1ccff373340eac78f8870\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"fulltext\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f5e29d134f6ae2f02fed940a\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fe8a34ad7e972c4f4e598847\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"采用单臂、前瞻性、II期临床试验设计。纳入标准为BCLC A–B期HCC、ECOG评分0–1、器官功能良好且在TACE后2周及MWA后1周影像学评估均达到mRECIST完全缓解的患者。排除既往接受过其他免疫调节剂、存在活动性感染或严重合并症者。所有患者在接受TACE和MWA后2周内开始接受特瑞普利单抗治疗，持续6个月。随访直至复发、死亡或研究结束。统计分析计划包括Kaplan-Meier估计RFS和OS，Cox比例风险模型计算HR，以及描述性统计次要终点。样本量计算基于历史数据预期中位RFS从15.5个月提升至27个月（HR=0.57），需30名参与者以检测显著差异。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b75b6c531806168ee3c5a352\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了针对特定亚群（BCLC A–B期，TACE+MWA后CR）的辅助免疫治疗标准化方案细节，包括药物剂量、疗程（6个月短程）、评估时间点及安全性监测流程。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为方案文件，缺乏实际临床结局数据；单臂设计无法提供因果推断证据，依赖外部历史数据进行比较；样本量较小（n=30），可能限制对罕见不良反应的检测能力及结果的普遍适用性；随访时间较短，无法评估长期“尾部效应”。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f516c5d011fc341d938ec983\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"当前材料为临床试验方案阶段\",\n          \"finding\": \"所给摘要未交代实际疗效数据、安全性结果或统计学结论。文中仅包含基于历史数据的预期结果（如预期RFS改善）和研究设计的理论依据。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0f17851423c5158ded11696c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"methods\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::6ac9ad2bebc7059ddafc25a8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"针对早期至中期HCC患者在接受TACE联合MWA等根治性局部治疗后面临高复发率（5年内高达70%）且缺乏标准化辅助治疗的问题，探究短程辅助PD-1抑制剂（特瑞普利单抗）是否能有效降低复发风险并改善预后，同时评估其安全性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2c32d64fd11413e8e7d895d8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象为巴塞罗那肝癌临床分期（BCLC）A–B期肝细胞癌（HCC）患者；情境为经动脉化疗栓塞（TACE）联合微波消融（MWA）局部治疗后达到完全缓解（CR）的高复发风险人群；范围聚焦于评估短期辅助免疫检查点抑制剂（特瑞普利单抗/Tislelizumab）的疗效与安全性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8830c3ef754ce06dd585ec36\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"本文是一篇单臂、前瞻性、II期临床试验方案，旨在评估在TACE联合MWA治疗BCLC A–B期HCC并确认完全缓解后，使用6个月短程辅助特瑞普利单抗（200 mg，每3周一次）的疗效和安全性。研究主要终点为无复发生存期（RFS），次要终点包括局部肿瘤进展、肝内远处复发、肝外疾病时间、总生存期及不良事件。该研究基于TACE诱导免疫原性细胞死亡与MWA协同作用产生有利免疫微环境的理论假设，试图验证短程辅助免疫治疗的可行性。由于这是一份试验方案（Protocol），目前尚未报告实际的患者入组数据或最终结果。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::7b77312891d3e4cc2ea696c0\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"仅提供方案设定，不提供疗效对比数据；不能证明该方案优于其他方案或观察性研究中的效果。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"明确了TACE联合MWA后辅助使用PD-1抑制剂的具体给药方案（特瑞普利单抗 200mg q3w x 6个月）及适用人群（BCLC A-B, CR状态）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0a3f8d22a54c5b8ceceaa816\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于文献引用的理论机制阐述，而非本研究实测的机制数据；不同介入方式（如RFA vs MWA）的效果可能存在差异，需注意外推限制。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"阐述了TACE和MWA通过诱导缺血、化疗毒性及热损伤导致免疫原性细胞死亡，释放肿瘤新抗原，从而重塑肿瘤免疫微环境并增强T细胞反应的机制假设。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0c606f0b8f28a6531283f01e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中指出目前尚无标准化的辅助治疗方案，IMbrave050等III期研究结果存在长期获益不维持的情况，且多数研究聚焦于手术切除而非消融/介入治疗后的辅助治疗。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::c09f082a0637e3742ebb9436\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"文中提到近期研究表明6个月的维持免疫治疗可提供与连续治疗相当的疗效，同时具有良好的安全性和依从性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::dc42c1b1a9a199905719b905\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究为单臂试验方案，无对照组，因此任何关于疗效的声称均为预期值或基于历史数据的推测，不能作为确证性证据。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1d752c6ac999e16ec53adf54\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象限定为BCLC A-B期且经TACE+MWA达到CR的患者，结果不可直接外推至其他分期、其他局部治疗方式（如单纯TACE或RFA）或未达CR的患者。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::03c28017ae4db0bbc863d9c7\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"机制部分主要引用自其他研究，本研究本身未进行生物标志物或机制层面的实证分析。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::2a0bc2e4ae20db7e5e41da89\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"所给材料未交代实际入组进度、脱落情况及最终安全性数据，无法评估真实世界的耐受性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::142a0121960c84ba03086ed3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0030\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-4dcc7c19ae5301df5638\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"caption_only\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"asset_id\": \"asset-24f387f49005f46578a2\",\n              \"kind\": \"asset\",\n              \"reason\": \"caption_or_locator_without_readable_image\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"assets\",\n              \"reason\": \"supplementaryFiles_fetch_transport_TimeoutError\",\n              \"status\": \"missing\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"fulltext\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::a54c4177705f169c0abc452e\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::fa917863b42b865823617a1e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4f68bc3c0e51d3eab948fccf\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ad5a28fe0d2f3d68b7b8e60f\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"1. 数据收集：使用公开可用的418名NSCLC患者基线肠道微生物组物种谱数据。2. 模型构建：训练机器学习模型预测ICI响应（R vs NR），固定参数，在保留测试集上验证（AUC=0.62，OS曲线差异显著p<0.0001）。3. 筛选子集：聚焦于模型预测价值良好的257名患者。4. 模拟干预：在模型中模拟健康供体FMT和治疗性菌群组合添加到患者基线微生物组中的过程，考察不同定植比例（exposure-dependent）对预测响应概率的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8dd8758eb8f26ba40de0493c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了一个基于基线微生物组预测ICI响应的机器学习框架，并证实了在特定患者亚群中，通过模拟FMT或定制菌群可提升预测响应率。\",\n          \"limits\": \"所给摘要未交代具体的机器学习算法类型、特征选择细节、治疗性菌群的具体组成成分、菌株分离的具体进展以及临床转化的时间表。仅基于回顾性数据的模拟，非前瞻性临床试验结果。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::89e7cfb984cc8f88cb8a9ce6\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"基于418名NSCLC患者数据的机器学习模型，在从未见过的测试集上\",\n          \"finding\": \"模型平均AUC为0.62，能显著区分总生存期（OS）曲线（p<0.0001）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::93a5dccbe3d93c3c7257faa4\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在模型预测价值良好的257名患者子集中，模拟健康供体FMT添加\",\n          \"finding\": \"FMT提高了模型预测的响应率，且效果依赖于暴露量（即FMT物种定植并替换患者基线微生物组的比例）。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a54ca17131fe904ae7af49e9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"key_findings\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"conditions\": \"在相同子集中，模拟候选治疗性菌群组合添加\",\n          \"finding\": \"候选治疗性菌群组合同样提高了响应率，且结果也呈现剂量/定植依赖性。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::679f65a7a246700078865033\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"paper_kind\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"empirical\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::b5b1d19764f6694dbdc7af78\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"problem_or_question\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"现有研究中单个微生物物种与ICI响应的关联往往不可重复且统计效力不足；虽然FMT显示有益，但药物开发多集中于简单菌群组合。本研究试图在模型中复制FMT的治疗益处，并设计能够增强ICI响应的治疗性微生物组合。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::ae8542404f12e8b138fd3320\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"research_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"基于418名非小细胞肺癌（NSCLC）患者的基线肠道微生物组数据，构建机器学习模型以预测免疫检查点抑制剂（ICI）的响应情况；并在模拟环境中评估粪菌移植（FMT）及设计型活细菌疗法对ICI疗效的影响。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4ae34442850db6176f0dc26c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"work_summary\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究旨在解决个体微生物物种与ICI响应关联缺乏统计稳健性的问题，并探索通过微生物组干预改善ICI疗效的策略。作者利用418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据训练了一个区分响应者（R）与非响应者（NR）的机器学习模型（AUC=0.62）。随后，在具有良好预测价值的子集（n=257）中，通过模拟实验评估了健康供体FMT和自定义治疗性菌群组合的效果。结果显示，增加FMT或治疗性菌群的定植比例可依赖性地提高模型预测的响应率。结论认为这些候选疗法有潜力改善ICI患者响应，目前正进行菌株分离培养以开发联合疗法。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::8ac1b1eac700149a344ed443\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"模型性能中等（AUC 0.62），且仅在NSCLC队列中验证，外推至其他实体瘤需谨慎。所给摘要未交代模型的可解释性（即哪些具体菌群驱动了预测）。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了基于全谱微生物组而非单一物种的ICI响应预测模型构建方法，并量化了模型性能（AUC 0.62）。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F1\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a23aef9604c65bbc592eb585\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"facet_contributions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"boundaries\": \"这是基于计算机模拟的结果，非体内或体外实验验证。所给摘要未交代具体的分子机制（如抗原呈递、炎症调节等），仅停留在表型预测层面。\",\n          \"contribution\": \"提出了通过“恢复响应者样微生物组特征”来克服ICI无响应的设计策略，并通过模拟证明了FMT和定制菌群的潜在有效性。\",\n          \"facet_id\": \"F2\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::9427443eb0fa7c8aa3845ea9\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"418名NSCLC患者的基线微生物组数据及其与ICI响应的统计关联分析。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::caf5e2a920fd8e6427e41f2c\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"broader_review_uses\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"material\": \"候选治疗性菌群的设计逻辑（围绕供体FMT和ICI响应相关物种及机制）及菌株分离培养的进展。\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::107cddc181c0ebe6140204b3\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"该研究仅为摘要级别，所有关于“治疗性菌群”的具体成分、作用机制及临床前/临床数据均未知，不得推断其具体功效或安全性。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::32be3241aa6be5e4aa9c6909\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"模型基于回顾性数据，模拟结果不代表真实临床疗效，需明确区分“预测模型中的响应率提升”与“实际患者生存获益”。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::1b85f9454a1366e32d8300b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"研究对象限定为NSCLC，其微生物组特征可能与其他实体瘤不同，跨癌种推广需谨慎。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::4c5791d22681d874f3bce1ab\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"review_planning_B\",\n          \"scope_interpretation_cautions\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"作者声称的“promise”为初步概念验证，尚处于菌株分离和培养阶段，距离实际应用仍有距离。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::674ce0ddf3f79ba2358a5d60\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0329\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"card_material\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"known_gaps\": [\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"identity\",\n              \"reason\": \"source identity was not independently verified\",\n              \"status\": \"input_attributed\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"no complete research body was indexed\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"kind\": \"coverage\",\n              \"reason\": \"only abstract or non-title snippets were available\",\n              \"status\": \"partial\"\n            }\n          ],\n          \"material_scope\": \"abstract_only\"\n        },\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::668c479a5777d8a189e172af\",\n          \"snapshot::7f4d4d07befb7d6373432503\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::f42355f065d836e3bfa3b47e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_depth\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"abstract\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5567ffc9b009ab7b1339d559\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::a5d09754fe44a730fc9e13b8\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"material_status\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"resolved\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5567ffc9b009ab7b1339d559\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::0cd9ce6812b543c46a2b0b3e\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"approach\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": \"文献综述与理论模型构建。作者通过总结现有文献中关于衰老相关微生物变化的研究，并结合已知的与ICIs响应相关的微生物标志物，进行对比分析。在此基础上，作者提出了一个概念性模型来解释观察到的广泛水平上的变化，并梳理了当前正在进行的针对老年群体的相关临床试验。\",\n        \"role\": \"evidence\",\n        \"snapshot_ids\": [\n          \"snapshot::5567ffc9b009ab7b1339d559\"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"atom_id\": \"atom::e6783c48b9261e1c8c710173\",\n        \"source_handle\": \"P0484\",\n        \"field_path\": [\n          \"study_summary_A\",\n          \"contribution_and_limits\"\n        ],\n        \"value\": {\n          \"contribution\": \"提供了将衰老微生物组变化与ICIs疗效联系起来的综合视角，提出了衰老可能通过改变微生物组导致ICIs疗效降低的假设性机制框架。\",\n          \"limits\": \"作为综述，其核心贡献在于总结和提出模型，而非提供新的实验证据或因果验证。所提出的机制和模型需要后续研究验证。材料未提供�